{"number":10,"title":"Exponents & Powers","slug":"exponents-and-powers","color":"","level":"","estTime":"","description":"Class 8 IMO — Exponents & powers: laws of exponents extended to integers, negative exponents, standard (scientific) form, and comparing very large and very small numbers.","topics":[{"title":"Laws of Exponents (Integers)","concept":"<p>The laws hold for integer exponents: <strong>aᵐ × aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ</strong>, <strong>aᵐ ÷ aⁿ = aᵐ⁻ⁿ</strong> and <strong>(aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ</strong>, with a⁰ = 1. So 2³ × 2⁻¹ = 2² = 4.</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Simplify 2³ × 2⁻¹.","solution":"2³⁻¹ = 2² = 4."},{"number":"2","problem":"Simplify (10³)².","solution":"10⁶."}],"recap":["aᵐ × aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ; aᵐ ÷ aⁿ = aᵐ⁻ⁿ; (aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ.","a⁰ = 1."],"quiz":[{"q":"Simplify 3² × 3³ as a power of 3.","options":["3⁵","3⁶","3¹","9⁵"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Add the exponents: 3²⁺³ = 3⁵.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is 5⁰?","options":["0","1","5","−1"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Any non-zero number to the power 0 is 1.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"}]},{"title":"Negative Exponents","concept":"<p>A <strong>negative exponent</strong> means the reciprocal: a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ. So 2⁻⁴ = 1/16 and 10⁻³ = 1/1000 = 0.001.</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Find 2⁻⁴.","solution":"1/2⁴ = 1/16."},{"number":"2","problem":"Find 10⁻³.","solution":"1/1000 = 0.001."}],"recap":["a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ.","10⁻¹ = 0.1, 10⁻² = 0.01, 10⁻³ = 0.001."],"quiz":[{"q":"What is 4⁻¹?","options":["4","¼","−4","16"],"correct":1,"explanation":"4⁻¹ = 1/4 = ¼.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is 2⁻³?","options":["6","8","1/8","−8"],"correct":2,"explanation":"2⁻³ = 1/2³ = 1/8.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]},{"title":"Standard Form & Comparing Numbers","concept":"<p><strong>Standard form</strong> writes a number as a × 10ⁿ, where 1 ≤ a &lt; 10. Large numbers use positive powers (75000 = 7.5 × 10⁴) and small numbers use negative powers (0.0003 = 3 × 10⁻⁴). The power of 10 tells which number is larger.</p>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Write 0.00045 in standard form.","solution":"4.5 × 10⁻⁴."},{"number":"2","problem":"Write 6,000,000 in standard form.","solution":"6 × 10⁶."}],"recap":["Standard form: a × 10ⁿ with 1 ≤ a < 10.","Large numbers → positive power; small numbers → negative power."],"quiz":[{"q":"Write 75000 in standard form.","options":["7.5 × 10³","7.5 × 10⁴","75 × 10³","7.5 × 10⁵"],"correct":1,"explanation":"75000 = 7.5 × 10⁴.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is 3 × 10⁻² as an ordinary number?","options":["0.3","0.03","0.003","300"],"correct":1,"explanation":"3 × 0.01 = 0.03.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"tests":{"online":{"title":"","minutes":18,"questions":[{"q":"aᵐ ÷ aⁿ equals a to the power ___ ?","options":["m + n","m − n","m × n","m/n"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Dividing powers of the same base subtracts the exponents.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"a⁻ⁿ equals ___ ?","options":["aⁿ","1/aⁿ","−aⁿ","n/a"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A negative exponent gives the reciprocal.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"a⁰ equals ___ ?","options":["0","1","a","−1"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Any non-zero number to the power 0 is 1.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Which is larger: 10³ or 10⁵?","options":["10³","10⁵","equal","cannot say"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A higher power of 10 is larger.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is 2³ × 2²?","options":["16","32","64","8"],"correct":1,"explanation":"2⁵ = 32.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is 3⁵ ÷ 3³?","options":["3","9","27","81"],"correct":1,"explanation":"3⁵⁻³ = 3² = 9.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is 2⁻⁴?","options":["1/8","1/16","16","−16"],"correct":1,"explanation":"2⁻⁴ = 1/2⁴ = 1/16.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is (10²)³?","options":["10⁵","10⁶","10⁸","10⁹"],"correct":1,"explanation":"10²ˣ³ = 10⁶.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is 5⁻²?","options":["1/10","1/25","25","−25"],"correct":1,"explanation":"5⁻² = 1/5² = 1/25.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is 4⁰ + 4¹?","options":["4","5","8","0"],"correct":1,"explanation":"1 + 4 = 5.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Write 0.00006 in standard form.","options":["6 × 10⁻⁴","6 × 10⁻⁵","6 × 10⁵","0.6 × 10⁻⁴"],"correct":1,"explanation":"0.00006 = 6 × 10⁻⁵.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Write 4,500,000 in standard form.","options":["4.5 × 10⁵","4.5 × 10⁶","45 × 10⁵","4.5 × 10⁷"],"correct":1,"explanation":"4,500,000 = 4.5 × 10⁶.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is 2⁵ × 2⁻² ÷ 2?","options":["2","4","8","16"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Exponents: 5 − 2 − 1 = 2, so 2² = 4.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"What is (3 × 10²) × (2 × 10³) as an ordinary number?","options":["60,000","600,000","6,000,000","6,000"],"correct":1,"explanation":"6 × 10⁵ = 600,000.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"}]}}}